        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: show cloud workspace conflicts in the Control UI",
        "body": "Related: #110224 (phase 3 of 3; phases 1 and 2 were #110952 and #111244)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nCompletes the operator-facing recovery path for cloud workspace conflicts. The Gateway already keeps local versions, applies non-conflicting cloud changes, preserves the cloud result under a staged Git ref, and records the conflict in the session; the Control UI previously left that recovery state hidden in raw placement and transcript data.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Control UI now turns the existing phase-2 conflict projection into a warning sidebar badge and a dismissible chat notice with a bounded path list, staged-result ref, and copyable inspect/take-cloud commands. The durable custom transcript entry renders as a structured conflict event, so the explanation remains visible after the live placement notice is cleared. No protocol or persistence shape changes are introduced in this phase.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can see that a cloud turn completed with workspace conflicts, identify which local paths were kept, inspect the staged cloud version, and deliberately take that version when appropriate. Non-conflicting cloud changes are already applied, and the UI explains deletion, file/directory obstruction, shell, and stale-ref cases without requiring a blind retry. Retained conflicts remain visible after reclaim and on child-session rows.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused Control UI proof: 3 files passed, 304 tests passed (`node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/components/session-row-badges.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/components/chat-message.test.ts`). The focused Gateway history projection suite also passed 181 tests.\n- Conflict-specific browser lifecycle proof on a synced Blacksmith Testbox at head `920bc1fa497`: 1 test passed in 2.53s. It rendered the live notice and sidebar badge, dismissed the notice while retaining structured history, reloaded a positively identified cleared session, and confirmed the badge/notice stayed absent while the durable history card remained. The three screenshot SHA-256 prefixes were `1518bb3a`, `a749df9b`, and `e7c91a4d`. [Testbox run](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29684690662)\n- Mantis also exercised the candidate Control UI browser shell and published its generic chat screenshot/recording. This is supplemental browser-environment evidence; the conflict-specific behavior is covered by the Testbox lifecycle test above. [Mantis artifacts](https://artifacts.openclaw.ai/mantis/web-ui-chat-proof/pr-111329/run-29684136714-1/index.json)\n- Structured AutoReview (`--mode branch --base origin/main`, Codex `gpt-5.6-sol`) is clean on head `920bc1fa497`, with no accepted/actionable findings and overall verdict `patch is correct` (0.88 confidence). The added browser test separately reviewed clean at 0.93 after its refreshed-session readiness race was fixed.\n- The rebase retained current-main inline approval cards and approval badges while adding the conflict UI. The landed phase-2 contract remains `workspaceResultConflict` / `cloud-workspace-conflict` with `paths`, `stagedResultRef`, and `totalCount`.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. The rebased diff was reviewed and validated before publication.\n",
